@H 1127_phi_coherence_link := "Round-2 / D2. Does joint faithful φ_EI track a CLASSICAL coherence/synchrony measure across the h1113/h1114 causal dyad — i.e. is integrated information predictable from cheap phase-coherence, or is it a distinct quantity? Sweep coupling strength and correlate joint φ_EI (exact MIP-EI, n=6) against (a) cross-channel phase-locking value and (b) mean pairwise |correlation|, across 10 seeds." :: universe [🟢 SUPPORTED-NUMERICAL — PHI-IS-DISTINCT (marginal, test-B)]
  seed         = "H_1114 🟢 (causal A→B link raises joint φ_EI 0.0032→0.0126, integration is channel-specific not correlation) + H_1120 🔴 (φ saturates with exchange rate) + H_1122 🔴 (φ is sign-blind to correlation). OPEN: is joint φ_EI just a re-encoding of classical coherence, or does it carry information coherence misses? If φ_EI ⟂ coherence at matched correlation, integration is a genuinely distinct ruler (strengthens a_phi_iit4_tool's no-proxy stance)."
  substrate    = "summer CPU $0 0-pod (toy n=6, 10 seeds). REUSE H_1114 dyad construction + faithful-Φ mirror VERBATIM (mirror≡stdlib n4/n5/n6 RE-PROVEN before scoring, BITS/log2, NO proxy). Coupling knob = COUP per-channel fold gain ∈ {0.00,0.10,0.20,0.30,0.45,0.60} (0=LINK-OFF, 0.30=H_1114 LINK-ON). Coherence = phase-locking value (PLV) over Hilbert-analytic channel pairs + mean |Pearson r|. g5/p7 deterministic."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-registered): 🟢 PHI-IS-DISTINCT iff at correlation-MATCHED coupling configs, joint φ_EI varies with d≥0.8 while PLV/|r| are statistically flat (φ carries info coherence misses) — OR φ_EI and PLV Spearman |ρ|<0.7 across the full sweep. 🔴 PHI-IS-COHERENCE-PROXY if φ_EI tracks PLV at ρ≥0.7 AND no correlation-matched dissociation (then cheap coherence predicts φ → φ adds nothing here)."
  result       = "🟢 PHI-IS-DISTINCT via test B (the φ–PLV decoupling disjunct). MIRROR RE-PROVEN ≡ stdlib BEFORE scoring: live `hexa run h1012_ref_faithful.hexa` n4/n5/n6 |Δ|≤8e-10, prove_mirrors_at_n {4:True,5:True}. SANITY GATE PASS: COUP=0.30 φ=0.012618 ≡ H_1114 LINK-ON (|Δ|=0.000000). SWEEP (φ_EI mean / PLV mean): COUP 0.00→0.003234/0.047 · 0.10→0.009344/0.237 · 0.20→0.011294/0.371 · 0.30→0.012618/0.449 · 0.45→0.013134/0.515 · 0.60→0.012829/0.550. φ–PLV Spearman: per-seed (n=60) ρ=+0.6558 (<0.7 frozen bar → test B PASS) ; arm-mean (n=6) ρ=+0.9429. φ–|r| per-seed ρ=+0.6303, arm-mean +0.9429. Test A FAIL: no PLV-flat arm-pair exists (every COUP step shifts PLV at d≥2.99) so a correlation-matched dissociation cannot be constructed. PROXY trigger=False. wall 60.3s."
  finding      = "At the toy n=6 dyad, cheap classical phase-coherence is an INCOMPLETE predictor of the exact MIP-EI φ. φ and PLV BOTH rise monotonically with coupling strength (arm-mean Spearman +0.94 — they co-trend at the ladder level), BUT the within-arm scatter of φ is decoupled from the within-arm scatter of PLV, dragging the per-seed φ–PLV Spearman to ρ=0.656, just under the 0.7 frozen bar. So coherence captures the coarse coupling-axis trend but misses the seed-to-seed structure φ_EI sees → integrated information is a (marginally) distinct ruler from synchrony here, supporting the a_phi_iit4_tool no-proxy stance."
  verdict_tier = "🟢 SUPPORTED-NUMERICAL (toy $0 CPU; reuses H_1114 dyad + Φ-mirror RE-PROVEN; frozen falsifier obeyed verbatim, test-B disjunct)"
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1127_phi_coherence_link/H_1127.txt · UNIVERSE/h1127_phi_coherence_link.py"
  honest       = "The green is the WEAKER of the two falsifier disjuncts: per-seed ρ=0.6558 only marginally clears <0.7, and the arm-mean φ–PLV co-trend is strong (+0.94). Test A (correlation-matched dissociation) was UNAVAILABLE — PLV separates every COUP arm too cleanly (d≥2.99) to hold flat — so distinctness rests solely on test B's within-arm decoupling. Distinctness HOLDS at this scale but is marginal, NOT a clean orthogonality; a tighter knob that holds PLV fixed while moving φ (or n>6 / real-socket dyad) would sharpen it. Toy n=6, faithful-only (big-Φ unscored cf H_1064); real-socket dyad-φ + production cells + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). p1-p6, metric = Spearman/Cohen-d (p7, NOT perplexity)."
  scope        = "Honest scope (a_scale_honest_scope): toy n=6 dyad, faithful-only (big-Φ unscored cf H_1064). Tests whether integration is a distinct ruler from classical synchrony at this scale; a 🟢 supports the no-proxy φ stance. p1-p6, metric = set-overlap/Spearman (p7, NOT perplexity)."
  xlink        = "h1114 (the dyad this reuses) · h1120 (rate saturation) · h1122 (sign-blindness) · a_phi_iit4_tool · a_paper_negative_ok"
